  "query_preview": "(Today through Tuesday)...\nIssued at 304 AM EDT Wed Jul 15 2026\n\nHigh pressure will continue to influence the weather over the region \nthrough at least Thursday, bringing hot and precipitation free \nconditions. Highs over the next few days are expected to reach the \nlow to mid 90s with heat indices near to slightly above 100 degrees. \nThe stagnant and suppressed air will also lead to greater ozone \nand lower air quality for parts of Indiana today. \n\nThe high pressure will start to break down by the end of the week, \nand models are showing better agreement on an upper wave bringing \ngood chances for showers and storms Friday. Aloft, NW flow will set \nup with a surface low prompting additional precip chances \nSaturday. After a brief break in PoPs, models show another system \nto move through early to mid next week with a decent chance of \ncooler temps moving in behind it.",
